{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-29182","model_call":49,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q2974"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q2974"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_570818059#3_1349217219","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2974","rank":4,"snippet":"3_1349217219\" , \"end_char\": 3140.000000 , \"headings\": \"Compulsive Shopping Compulsive Shopping What Is Compulsive Shopping? Understanding Compulsive Shopping Key Takeaways Diagnosing Compulsive Shopping Example of Compulsive Shopping Treatment for Compulsive Shopping \" , \"segment\": \"It can also be a symptom of serious mental ailments, such as bipolar disorder. Therapy and antidepressant medication can help in the treatment of compulsive shopping. Diagnosing Compulsive Shopping Compulsive shoppers typically are insecure people with low self-esteem and low <cover>impulse control. Not surprisingly, people with mood, anxiety, and eating disorders often exhibit symptoms. Sometimes compulsive shopping </cover>can also manifest itself as part of a much more severe illness, such as obsessive-compulsive disorder. 1 ﻿ Much as bulimics will purge meals after overeating, compulsive shoppers are known to throw away their purchases. Some research shows a link between attention deficit disorders and compulsive shopping. 3 ﻿ Circumstantial factors have also been found to cause compulsive shopping behavior. Examples of such circumstances include avoidance coping, negation, and isolating factors. 4 ﻿ Compulsive shopping is not the same as retail therapy, the occasional shopping binge in which many people indulge.\" , \""},"time":10},"model_calls":49,"document_judgments":39,"relevance_3":12,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
