{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-29182","model_call":50,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ emotions influence purchase decisions)"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ emotions influence purchase decisions)"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_31_872412108#10_1758052581","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q2975","rank":1,"snippet":"B2B Marketing Case Study Marketing Best Practices for B2B Brands 22. Postcards Pros of Postcard Marketing for B2B Cons of Postcard Marketing for B2B Postcard Marketing Best Practices for B2B Marketing 23. Direct Mail Marketing Pros of Direct Mail for B2B Marketing Cons of Direct Mail for B2B Marketing Direct Mail Marketing Best Practices for B2B Brands Customer Experience (CX): The Golden Thread That Ties B2B Marketing Strategies Together B2B Marketing Strategies: Choose Yours Wisely \" , \"segment\": \"This means purchase decisions are mainly based on facts and logic. In B2C circles, <cover>emotions drive personas and influence purchase decisions </cover>so the deal happens fast. 3. Strategies Generally, because B2B buyers usually decide based on facts and logic, marketers build tactics around educating their target audience. While B2C marketing also involves educating, it’s not always necessary. In this vertical, edutainment that tugs at the emotions works better. 4. Purchase Process Fourthly, B2B buyers have to confer with decision-makers before making a purchase and usually prefer working with an account manager during and after purchase. By comparison, B2C buyers rarely have to discuss their purchase decision with anyone and prefer to purchase directly. 5.\" ,"},"time":296},"model_calls":50,"document_judgments":40,"relevance_3":12,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
