{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-29182","model_call":54,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ mood affect spending behavior)"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ mood affect spending behavior)"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_14_44183134#1_106884776","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q2978","rank":1,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_14_44183134#1_106884776\" , \"end_char\": 2055.000000 , \"headings\": \"Four Tips To Ease Your Mood Swings Four Tips To Ease Your Mood Swings What Causes Mood Swings? Do Hormones <cover>Affect Behavior? Teens and Hormones Women and Hormones Other Causes of Mood Swings How To Reduce Mood Swings’ Symptoms? 1. Purge The Bad 2. Take A Moment To Chill 3. Seek Balance 4. Switch It Up When To Seek Help? \" , \"segment\": \"For example, spending </cover>too much time at work and being away from your family for extended periods of time, can lead to mood swings. A lack of sleep, eating an unhealthy diet and excessive use of drugs and alcohol can also cause drastic changes in your emotions. However, when the underlying cause is addressed, mood swings usually dissipate. Do Hormones Affect Behavior? Teens and Hormones Teens experience changes in their hormones during puberty. These evolving hormone systems can wreak havoc on a young person’s brain and cause a change in their behavior. Women and Hormones Women experience mood swings twice as "},"time":315},"model_calls":54,"document_judgments":44,"relevance_3":12,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
